# CakePHP Migrations

## Plugin semantics

`cakephp/migrations` owns versioned schema migrations and seeds via `bin/cake migrations` (builtin backend on modern versions). Prefer migrations over ad-hoc production SQL when the plugin is installed.

## Required behavior

- Apply only when `cakephp/migrations` ^4/^5 is installed.
- Put schema changes in migration classes under the project’s Migrations path.
- Keep migrations focused on schema (and intentional data migrations); do not bury app business rules here.
- Do not invent Laravel `artisan migrate` / Eloquent migration APIs.

## Anti-patterns

- Hand-editing production schema with no migration when Migrations is the project standard
- Inventing Artisan migration commands
- Mixing large unrelated schema changes in one opaque migration without cause
